    counter (independent of m_clk) drives all rate-based stats, and 2) a
    reset_stats() method to be called after warmup so collected stats are only
    for post-warmup. The "cycles" stat now reports m_measured_clk.
    The latency-throughput frontend exposes a warmup reset hook so traffic
    generators can mark the start of the measured window.
    
    README updates clarify the fast vs full lat-tp flow, document the new
    config shape (COMMON_CONFIG + per-suite request counts), and fix a few
    typos.

